- is all Broadway?
- I grew up,

00:00:03.326 --> 00:00:04.159
it's all Broadway

00:00:04.159 --> 00:00:05.760
and I've always wanted to do this record.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:06.840
- Yeah.
- It for me

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.040
it has been the most

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.930
and I know you've had
these kinds of records

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:12.120
that feel the most vocally exciting

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:12.953
- Yeah.
- and the most

00:00:12.953 --> 00:00:15.200
vocally expansive, especially
because as artists,

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.300
sometimes if we get pegged with one sound.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.040
- 100%, that's why I
love Christmas albums,

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:19.873
you can do whatever there.
- Yeah, me too,

00:00:19.873 --> 00:00:20.890
you could do whatever you
want and nobody says anything.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:21.723
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:21.723 --> 00:00:23.488
- Okay, nobody cries, nobody
fusses, nobody whines.

00:00:23.488 --> 00:00:24.770
- Yeah, yeah.
- Exactly.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:25.603
- Just sounds classic, yeah.

00:00:25.603 --> 00:00:26.436
- So I've always wanted to do this

00:00:26.436 --> 00:00:27.810
'cause I grew up doing theater.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:28.850
- Yeah.
- I grew up, you know,

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:32.030
in community theater and
high school and college

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:34.130
all throughout and always
really wanted to get back to it.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.820
Super thankful for the
success I had as a musician,

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:37.840
- Yeah.
- but also thankful

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.240
that that success has let me enter into

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.920
then the theater community at a place

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.010
- Yeah.
- 'cause you came and saw me,

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:45.160
years ago, like
- Yes, I did.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:45.993
- in Chicago.
- And you were

00:00:45.993 --> 00:00:46.826
freaking awesome

00:00:46.826 --> 00:00:47.800
and I've always wanted to,

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:49.000
I'm a nerd for Broadway too,

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:49.833
I grew up with
- I know you are!

00:00:49.833 --> 00:00:50.666
- musical theater

00:00:50.666 --> 00:00:53.790
and so I am envious of this whole project

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:57.050
and I was envious and just
so elated for you as well.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.309
- Thank you.
- You shine so bright.

00:00:58.309 --> 00:00:59.142
- Yeah, you get it though.
- It was so good.

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:00.950
- It's like it, it holds
a place in your heart

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:02.440
and it really I think informs--

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:03.940
- It's a hard thing to do too,

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:04.773
Broadway is hard

00:01:04.773 --> 00:01:06.250
- Yeah.
- like it's a big schedule.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:07.900
- It's an, yes it is--
- If you can nail that

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:08.733
you're amazing.

00:01:08.733 --> 00:01:09.708
- It's a big schedule.

00:01:09.708 --> 00:01:10.541
- Yeah.

00:01:10.541 --> 00:01:12.730
- But it's just so
enriching and so worth it

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.330
and I think, you know, the music itself

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:15.880
just as you're saying is,

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:18.190
it's so informative as an artist

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:19.760
and I know you get this
too as a performer,

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:21.170
you know you learn about what it is

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:22.740
to be a character in a song,

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:25.136
you learn about what it is to embody that.

00:01:25.136 --> 00:01:27.560
- It's not that far from country to me.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:28.393
- It's all storytelling.
- Like country music

00:01:28.393 --> 00:01:29.226
is all storytelling.

00:01:29.226 --> 00:01:30.220
- It's all storytelling.
- Yeah.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:31.760
That's why when everybody, yeah they said

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:32.593
you were doing the album.
- For sure.

00:01:32.593 --> 00:01:33.880
I was like, well it's
like more storytelling.

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:34.713
- Obviously.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:34.713 --> 00:01:35.980
- Not a big leap.
- Yeah.

